+This software depends on libsignal-protocol-c which is covered by a [separate license](https://github.com/whispersystems/libsignal-protocol-c#license).
+
+## Opt-in OMEMO2 API
+
+This local fork provides a separate `OMEMO2Context`, `OMEMO2IdentityKeyPair`,
+`OMEMO2KeyPair`, `OMEMO2Bundle`, `OMEMO2Ciphertext` and `OMEMO2Session` for the
+cryptographic profile in XEP-0384 0.9.1, `urn:xmpp:omemo:2`. It requires the
+companion SignalProtocolC fork with `omemo_keys.h`, `omemo_wire.h` and
+`omemo_session.h`. Both forks must be pinned together when distributing an app.
+
+Existing `SignalContext`, `SignalStorage`, builder/cipher APIs and Signal record
+formats retain their legacy behavior. Switching a namespace or selecting a new
+pod version does not activate OMEMO2 in an application.
+
+- Identity wire keys are raw 32-byte Ed25519. Fingerprints are raw 32-byte
+  X25519. The local identity private key is an X25519 scalar, not an Ed25519 seed.
+- Bundle construction validates keys and an EdDSA-compatible SPK signature.
+  Both SPK and OPK IDs must be in `1...2147483647`, as required by §5.3.2.
+  Identity trust is checked by the application before beginning a session.
+- `initiateSessionWithIdentity:bundle:error:` creates an initiator session.
+  `acceptKeyExchange:...plaintext:error:` returns a responder session and the
+  first plaintext only after authenticating the incoming exchange.
+- Encrypt 48 bytes (`payload key || payload MAC`) or 32 zero bytes for an empty
+  OMEMO control message. `OMEMO2Ciphertext.isKeyExchange` determines the XMPP
+  `kex` flag. The same EK and an increasing message counter are retained on
+  repeated outgoing KEX until an authenticated reply confirms the exchange.
+- Parsing `OMEMO2Ciphertext` validates protobuf syntax but does not authenticate
+  the message. Use `decryptCiphertext:error:` for authentication. Failed parsing,
+  authentication and replay leave the existing session state unchanged.
+- Persist `serializedDataWithError:` in protected, profile-specific storage.
+  Restore it with `restoreSessionWithData:error:`. Legacy Signal records cannot
+  be restored through this API. Storage updates, OPK consumption and accepting
+  an incoming message must be committed atomically by the caller; retain the old
+  snapshot if storage fails. Concurrent operations are synchronized within a
+  context, while multiple restored objects require caller coordination.
+
+The application still owns XMPP envelopes, bundle/device publication, identity
+trust, OPK refill/removal, SPK rotation, ACK/heartbeat scheduling, migration,
+protected persistence and coordinated deployment with other clients. These
+wrappers provide the cryptographic dependency layer.
+
+`Testing/SignalProtocolTests/OMEMO2Tests.m` contains the dedicated XCTest suite.
+Enable it in a Podfile with `:testspecs => ['OMEMO2']` on the local
+`SignalProtocolObjC` dependency.
